      "for": "2114761816199098587",
      "draft_en": "The key stat in today's Anthropic S-1 chatter, via @levie: the average Fortune 500 customer spends less than 0.1% of its expenses on Anthropic.\n\nRead that as a marketer.\n\nAI is about to make 100x more of your ads, not 100x fewer. Creative volume goes up. Review headcount does not.\n\nThe bottleneck moves from making the ad to proving it's safe to publish: brand rules, legal claims, platform policy.\n\nThat's the layer we're building at Aubric.",
      "video_tip": "20s vertical, talking head. Hold up a phone with the stat on screen ('<0.1%'), then cut to a counter ticking from 10 ads to 10,000 ads while a single 'Reviewer' avatar stays fixed. End on an Aubric verdict card: APPROVE / FIX / BLOCK."
    },
    {
      "angle": "'X is never the reason' myth-bust (rides @AlexHormozi)",
      "for": "2114843234375786581",
      "draft_en": "\"The platform changed its policy\" is never the real reason your ad got rejected.\n\nPolicies are written down. If you check every creative against them before you hit publish, policy updates barely touch you.\n\nOne exception: new laws. Pennsylvania's AI Deceptive Advertising Act takes effect Dec 21, and AI-generated or significantly altered ads need a disclosure.\n\nOtherwise, just check your work before the algorithm does.",
      "video_tip": "15s vertical. Open on a red 'Ad rejected' notification. Text overlay: 'It wasn't the algorithm.' Cut to a checklist animating through brand rule, claim, platform policy, PA law (Dec 21). Close with a green 'Approved before publish' stamp."
    },
    {
      "angle": "New-era launch frame (rides @sama's 'new era of computer use')",
      "for": "2114818620782248024",
      "draft_en": "Computer use is here. Agents can now click buttons for you.\n\nIncluding the \"Publish\" button in your ad account.\n\nWhen an agent ships 500 ad variants overnight, who checked the claims, the logo usage, the disclosures, and the platform policy?\n\nThe new era needs a gate between the agent and the publish button.\n\nWho's building that in your stack?",
      "video_tip": "15s screen recording style. A cursor (labelled 'AI agent') glides toward a big 'Publish' button in an ad manager mockup. Freeze frame one pixel before the click; Aubric card slides in: 'Checking 500 variants... 12 need fixes, 3 blocked.' End text: 'Gate before publish.'"
